blockers:
claim: Use-after-free bug in onFrame callback: frame is stack-owned by caller and copied by value, but the lambda captures only the copy by value while the original frame data pointer (frame->data) points to memory that becomes invalid after the callback returns. The frame->data[64] array is stack-allocated in the mock worker and becomes invalid once onFrame returns.; file: app/qttunebridge.cpp; quote: const qttune_frame_t copy = *frame;   // frame is stack-owned by mock_worker

    QMetaObject::invokeMethod(self, [self, copy]() {
        self->handleFrameInternal(&copy);
    }, Qt::QueuedConnection);

claim: Thread safety violation: M_QML signal emission is not thread-safe. QML/Qt objects must only be accessed from the GUI thread. The onFrame callback is invoked from a worker thread and directly emits signals without proper thread marshaling.; file: app/qttunebridge.cpp; quote: void QtTuneBridge::onFrame(const qttune_frame_t* frame, void* user_data)
{
    QtTuneBridge* self = static_cast<QtTuneBridge*>(user_data);
    if (frame == nullptr || self == nullptr) {
        return;
    }
    if (!self->m_connected.load(std::memory_order_acquire)) {
        return;
    }
    if (self->m_currentFrameCount >= FrameListModel::MaxFrames) {
        self->m_droppedFrames.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
        return;
    }

claim: Race condition on m_currentFrameCount: This variable is accessed from both the worker thread (in onFrame) and the GUI thread without any synchronization. It is read in connectSession and modified in onFrame without atomic protection.; file: app/qttunebridge.cpp; quote: if (self->m_currentFrameCount >= FrameListModel::MaxFrames) {
        self->m_droppedFrames.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
        return;
    }

claim: Buffer overflow risk: frame->data_length is used directly as the size for QByteArray construction without bounds checking. If data_length > 64 (the size of the data array), this would read beyond the array bounds.; file: app/qttunebridge.cpp; quote: vm["payloadHex"] = QByteArray(
        reinterpret_cast<const char*>(frame->data),
        static_cast<qsizetype>(frame->data_length)).toHex();

